# Test helpers (owned by test-engineer; signatures are stable, ask the lead before changing one)

Run anything that touches the DB as `bash ../scripts/with-db.sh npx vitest run <path>` from `./app`.
Env comes from `.env.local` (then `.env`) via `vitest.config.mts`. `tests/setup/global.ts` points
`TEST_BASE_URL` at a live Next server (3000, else it starts `next dev -p 3100` and stops it after).
Test files run one at a time (`fileParallelism: false`); tests inside a file are sequential unless you use `Promise.all`.

| module | export | what it does |
|---|---|---|
| `env.ts` | `env.supabaseUrl / publishableKey / secretKey / databaseUrl / gatewayKey / seedPassword / baseUrl` | typed, lazy env getters (throw if missing) |
| `clients.ts` | `anonClient()` | supabase-js with the publishable key, no user |
| | `userClient(accessToken)` | publishable key + `Authorization: Bearer <token>` (PostgREST, RPC, Storage as that user) |
| | `adminClient()` | secret key (setup only: auth admin, storage cleanup) |
| `db.ts` | `pool()`, `sql<T>(text, params)` | pg pool on DATABASE_URL as `postgres` (bypasses RLS). int8 -> number (throws if unsafe), date -> `"YYYY-MM-DD"` string. Call `closePool()` in `afterAll` |
| | `newConnection(): Promise<pg.Client>` | a separate connected session for race tests; `await c.end()` yourself |
| `seeded.ts` | `SEEDED` | key -> email of the 7 brief accounts: `northwindManager, northwindStaff, aisyah, ben, probe, betaManager, chen` |
| | `signIn(email, password = SEED_PASSWORD, { fresh? }) -> { userId, email, accessToken }` | real password grant; cached in memory + `node_modules/.cache` while the token has >10 min left and its auth.sessions row still exists. `fresh: true` for a test that signs out |
| | `seeded(key)`, `ctxFor(key) -> { userId }` | sign in a seeded account / ctx for calling services directly |
| `http.ts` | `api(token?)` -> `{ get(path), post(path, body?), request(method, path, body?) }` | route handlers over HTTP with `Authorization: Bearer`, `redirect: 'manual'`; returns `{ status, body, headers }` (body = parsed JSON, else text). A string body is sent verbatim. `opts.headers` adds headers (e.g. `Idempotency-Key`) |
| | `postForm(path, fields | pairs)` | x-www-form-urlencoded POST, no auth (webhook) |
| `gateway.ts` | `gatewaySignature(fields, key?)`, `gatewayPaidAt(date)`, `signedCallback(billId, amountSen, paid, extra?, key?)` | brief §5 signature written independently of the app |
| `fixtures.ts` | `createFixtureOrg({ name?, units = 2, lease?, leaseTenant = 'A' }) -> FixtureOrg` | fresh org: manager + staff memberships, units, tenants A/B linked to fresh auth users (`*@fixture.test`, SEED_PASSWORD, signed in). `lease` inserts a lease on `unitIds[0]` + exactly `generateSchedule(lease)` invoices. Returns `{ orgId, orgName, unitIds, tenantAId, tenantBId, users: {manager, staff, tenantA, tenantB}, tokens: {...}, lease?: { id, ..., invoices: [{ id, ...ScheduledInvoice }] } }` |
| | `insertLease(orgId, unitId, tenantId, lease, createdBy?)`, `insertUnit(orgId, name?)`, `insertTenant(orgId, userId, fullName, email)`, `createFixtureUser(label)` | building blocks (direct pg, no audit rows) |
| `time.ts` | `asOf(isoWithOffset)`, `mytAt(date, "HH:MM[:SS]")`, `mytMidnight(date)`, `mytEndOfDay(date)` | deterministic instants; `asOf` rejects naive strings |
| `contract.ts` | `errorBody`, `idBody`, `recordPaymentBody`, `statusBody`, `leaseDetail` (+ `leaseDto`/`invoiceDto`/`paymentDto`), `collectionsBody` | strict zod schemas of SPEC's HTTP bodies, written from SPEC (never imported from the app) |
| | `uploadSlip(token, orgId, leaseId) -> path` | uploads a real PDF to `payment-slips/<org>/<lease>/<uuid>.pdf` as that user (UI path); throws if Storage refuses |

`tests/setup/global.ts` also runs `npm run seed` once when `manager@northwind.test` is missing from auth.users
(fast gate: reset, then tests), and fails setup if the seed fails.

Fixtures are never deleted (D29: payments and audit_log are append-only); use random names.
Never insert payments/allocations directly to set up a scenario you then assert on: go through the API or the
`private.*` functions so the rows are the ones the app would produce.
import { randomUUID } from "node:crypto";
import { generateSchedule, type ScheduledInvoice } from "@/lib/billing";
import { adminClient } from "./clients";
import { pool } from "./db";
import { env } from "./env";
import { signIn, type Session } from "./seeded";

// Fixture orgs are never deleted (D29: audit_log and payments are append-only by design); every
// fixture uses random names/emails so tests never collide and never touch the seeded data.
// Rows are written with pg as `postgres` (bypasses RLS) against the T1 schema names in SPEC.md.

export type FixtureRole = "manager" | "staff" | "tenantA" | "tenantB";

export interface LeaseInput {
  startDate: string;
  endDate: string;
  monthlyRentSen: number;
  depositSen: number;
}

export interface FixtureInvoice extends ScheduledInvoice {
  id: string;
}

export interface FixtureLease extends LeaseInput {
  id: string;
  orgId: string;
  unitId: string;
  tenantId: string;
  /** Exactly generateSchedule(lease), in its order, with the inserted ids. */
  invoices: FixtureInvoice[];
}

export interface FixtureOrg {
  orgId: string;
  orgName: string;
  /** Unit ids, in creation order (default 2 units). */
  unitIds: string[];
  /** tenants.id rows linked (tenants.user_id) to users.tenantA / users.tenantB. */
  tenantAId: string;
  tenantBId: string;
  users: Record<FixtureRole, Session>;
  /** Shorthand for users[role].accessToken. */
  tokens: Record<FixtureRole, string>;
  /** Present when opts.lease was given: a lease on unitIds[0] for tenant A (or opts.leaseTenant). */
  lease?: FixtureLease;
}

export interface FixtureOpts {
  name?: string;
  units?: number;
  lease?: LeaseInput;
  leaseTenant?: "A" | "B";
}

const rand = () => randomUUID().slice(0, 8);

/** Creates a confirmed auth user with SEED_PASSWORD via the Admin API and signs it in for real. */
export async function createFixtureUser(label: string): Promise<Session> {
  const email = `${label}-${rand()}@fixture.test`.toLowerCase();
  const { error } = await adminClient().auth.admin.createUser({
    email,
    password: env.seedPassword,
    email_confirm: true,
  });
  if (error) throw new Error(`createUser(${email}) failed: ${error.message}`);
  return signIn(email, env.seedPassword);
}

/**
 * Inserts a lease and exactly generateSchedule(lease) as its invoices, in one transaction,
 * directly with pg (no audit row; this is setup, not the createLease code path under test).
 */
export async function insertLease(
  orgId: string,
  unitId: string,
  tenantId: string,
  lease: LeaseInput,
  createdBy: string | null = null,
): Promise<FixtureLease> {
  const schedule = generateSchedule(lease);
  const client = await pool().connect();
  try {
    await client.query("begin");
    const { rows } = await client.query<{ id: string }>(
      `insert into public.leases (org_id, unit_id, tenant_id, start_date, end_date, monthly_rent_sen, deposit_sen, created_by)
       values ($1, $2, $3, $4::date, $5::date, $6, $7, $8) returning id`,
      [orgId, unitId, tenantId, lease.startDate, lease.endDate, lease.monthlyRentSen, lease.depositSen, createdBy],
    );
    const leaseId = rows[0].id;
    const invoices: FixtureInvoice[] = [];
    for (const inv of schedule) {
      const r = await client.query<{ id: string }>(
        `insert into public.invoices (org_id, lease_id, kind, period_index, period_start, period_end, due_date, amount_sen)
         values ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5::date, $6::date, $7::date, $8) returning id`,
        [orgId, leaseId, inv.kind, inv.periodIndex, inv.periodStart, inv.periodEnd, inv.dueDate, inv.amountSen],
      );
      invoices.push({ ...inv, id: r.rows[0].id });
    }
    await client.query("commit");
    return { id: leaseId, orgId, unitId, tenantId, ...lease, invoices };
  } catch (e) {
    await client.query("rollback").catch(() => undefined);
    throw e;
  } finally {
    client.release();
  }
}

/** Adds one more unit to an org (random name unless given). */
export async function insertUnit(orgId: string, name = `U-${rand()}`): Promise<string> {
  const { rows } = await pool().query<{ id: string }>(
    "insert into public.units (org_id, name) values ($1, $2) returning id",
    [orgId, name],
  );
  return rows[0].id;
}

/** Adds a tenant row (optionally linked to an auth user) to an org. */
export async function insertTenant(orgId: string, userId: string | null, fullName: string, email: string): Promise<string> {
  const { rows } = await pool().query<{ id: string }>(
    "insert into public.tenants (org_id, user_id, full_name, email) values ($1, $2, $3, $4) returning id",
    [orgId, userId, fullName, email],
  );
  return rows[0].id;
}

/**
 * A fresh, isolated organization: manager + staff (memberships), units, two tenants linked to
 * their own auth users, optionally a lease (unit 0, tenant A by default) with its invoices.
 * Every user is real (Admin API) and signed in with the password grant.
 */
export async function createFixtureOrg(opts: FixtureOpts = {}): Promise<FixtureOrg> {
  const tag = rand();
  const orgName = opts.name ?? `Fixture Org ${tag}`;
  const [manager, staff, tenantA, tenantB] = await Promise.all([
    createFixtureUser(`manager-${tag}`),
    createFixtureUser(`staff-${tag}`),
    createFixtureUser(`tenanta-${tag}`),
    createFixtureUser(`tenantb-${tag}`),
  ]);

  const { rows: orgRows } = await pool().query<{ id: string }>(
    "insert into public.organizations (name) values ($1) returning id",
    [orgName],
  );
  const orgId = orgRows[0].id;
  await pool().query(
    "insert into public.memberships (user_id, org_id, role) values ($1, $3, 'manager'), ($2, $3, 'staff')",
    [manager.userId, staff.userId, orgId],
  );
  const unitIds: string[] = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < (opts.units ?? 2); i++) unitIds.push(await insertUnit(orgId, `U${i + 1}-${tag}`));
  const tenantAId = await insertTenant(orgId, tenantA.userId, `Tenant A ${tag}`, tenantA.email);
  const tenantBId = await insertTenant(orgId, tenantB.userId, `Tenant B ${tag}`, tenantB.email);

  const users = { manager, staff, tenantA, tenantB };
  const fx: FixtureOrg = {
    orgId,
    orgName,
    unitIds,
    tenantAId,
    tenantBId,
    users,
    tokens: {
      manager: manager.accessToken,
      staff: staff.accessToken,
      tenantA: tenantA.accessToken,
      tenantB: tenantB.accessToken,
    },
  };
  if (opts.lease) {
    if (unitIds.length === 0) throw new Error("createFixtureOrg: a lease needs at least one unit");
    const tenantId = opts.leaseTenant === "B" ? tenantBId : tenantAId;
    fx.lease = await insertLease(orgId, unitIds[0], tenantId, opts.lease, manager.userId);
  }
  return fx;
}
import { createHash } from "node:crypto";
import { mkdirSync, readFileSync, renameSync, writeFileSync } from "node:fs";
import path from "node:path";
import pg from "pg";
import { anonClient } from "./clients";
import { env } from "./env";

/** The 7 seeded accounts from the brief (npm run seed). All share SEED_PASSWORD. */
export const SEEDED = {
  northwindManager: "manager@northwind.test",
  northwindStaff: "staff@northwind.test",
  aisyah: "aisyah@northwind.test",
  ben: "ben@northwind.test",
  probe: "probe@northwind.test",
  betaManager: "manager@beta.test",
  chen: "chen@beta.test",
} as const;
export type SeededKey = keyof typeof SEEDED;

export interface Session {
  userId: string;
  email: string;
  accessToken: string;
}

// GoTrue rate-limits /token per IP (150 burst, then 1 per 2 s locally). Real sign-ins are cached
// in-process and on disk (node_modules/.cache) and reused only while the token has > 10 min left
// AND its session row still exists for the same user (so a db reset or sign-out invalidates it).
const CACHE_DIR = path.join(process.cwd(), "node_modules", ".cache", "rent-tests-sessions");
const MIN_TTL_S = 600;
const memo = new Map<string, Session>();

interface JwtClaims {
  sub: string;
  exp: number;
  session_id?: string;
}

function claims(token: string): JwtClaims {
  const part = token.split(".")[1] ?? "";
  return JSON.parse(Buffer.from(part, "base64url").toString("utf8")) as JwtClaims;
}

function cacheFile(email: string, password: string): string {
  const h = createHash("sha256").update(`${env.supabaseUrl}|${email}|${password}`).digest("hex");
  return path.join(CACHE_DIR, `${h.slice(0, 32)}.json`);
}

async function stillValid(s: Session): Promise<boolean> {
  let c: JwtClaims;
  try {
    c = claims(s.accessToken);
  } catch {
    return false;
  }
  if (c.sub !== s.userId || c.exp - Date.now() / 1000 < MIN_TTL_S || !c.session_id) return false;
  const client = new pg.Client({ connectionString: env.databaseUrl });
  try {
    await client.connect();
    const r = await client.query(
      `select 1 from auth.sessions s join auth.users u on u.id = s.user_id
        where s.id = $1 and u.id = $2 and lower(u.email) = lower($3)`,
      [c.session_id, s.userId, s.email],
    );
    return (r.rowCount ?? 0) === 1;
  } catch {
    return false;
  } finally {
    await client.end().catch(() => undefined);
  }
}

function readCache(file: string): Session | undefined {
  try {
    return JSON.parse(readFileSync(file, "utf8")) as Session;
  } catch {
    return undefined;
  }
}

function writeCache(file: string, s: Session): void {
  try {
    mkdirSync(CACHE_DIR, { recursive: true });
    const tmp = `${file}.${process.pid}.tmp`;
    writeFileSync(tmp, JSON.stringify(s));
    renameSync(tmp, file); // atomic, so parallel workers never read half a file
  } catch {
    // cache is an optimisation only
  }
}

async function passwordGrant(email: string, password: string): Promise<Session> {
  for (let attempt = 0; ; attempt++) {
    const { data, error } = await anonClient().auth.signInWithPassword({ email, password });
    if (!error && data.session && data.user) {
      return { userId: data.user.id, email, accessToken: data.session.access_token };
    }
    const rateLimited = error?.status === 429 || /rate limit/i.test(error?.message ?? "");
    if (!rateLimited || attempt >= 20) {
      throw new Error(`signIn(${email}) failed: ${error?.status ?? ""} ${error?.message ?? "no session"}`);
    }
    await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 3_000));
  }
}

/**
 * Real Supabase password sign-in (no mocks). Returns the user's id and access token.
 * `password` defaults to SEED_PASSWORD. Pass `{ fresh: true }` to bypass the cache
 * (e.g. a test that signs the session out afterwards).
 */
export async function signIn(
  email: string,
  password: string = env.seedPassword,
  opts: { fresh?: boolean } = {},
): Promise<Session> {
  const file = cacheFile(email, password);
  if (!opts.fresh) {
    const hit = memo.get(file) ?? readCache(file);
    if (hit && (await stillValid(hit))) {
      memo.set(file, hit);
      return hit;
    }
  }
  const s = await passwordGrant(email, password);
  if (!opts.fresh) {
    memo.set(file, s);
    writeCache(file, s);
  }
  return s;
}

/** Sign in one of the seeded accounts by key, e.g. `await seeded('aisyah')`. */
export function seeded(key: SeededKey): Promise<Session> {
  return signIn(SEEDED[key]);
}

/** `{ userId }` ctx for calling services directly (src/server/services/**) as a real seeded user. */
export async function ctxFor(key: SeededKey): Promise<{ userId: string }> {
  const s = await seeded(key);
  return { userId: s.userId };
}
import pg from "pg";
import { env } from "./env";

// Direct Postgres access as the `postgres` owner (DATABASE_URL). For fixtures, catalog checks
// (information_schema / pg_catalog) and asserting DB state. Never used to reset the DB.

// Per-connection type parsers (never the global pg.types, which Prisma's adapter-pg also uses):
// int8 -> number when it is a safe integer (money is bigint sen, D3); date -> raw "YYYY-MM-DD"
// string, never a local-time Date (TZ-independent).
const INT8 = 20;
const DATE = 1082;
const types: pg.CustomTypesConfig = {
  getTypeParser: ((oid: number, format?: "text" | "binary") => {
    if (oid === INT8)
      return (v: string) => {
        const n = Number(v);
        if (!Number.isSafeInteger(n)) throw new Error(`int8 ${v} is not a safe integer`);
        return n;
      };
    if (oid === DATE) return (v: string) => v;
    return pg.types.getTypeParser(oid, format ?? "text");
  }) as pg.CustomTypesConfig["getTypeParser"],
};

let shared: pg.Pool | undefined;

/** Shared pool for the current test file (max 5). Call closePool() in afterAll. */
export function pool(): pg.Pool {
  shared ??= new pg.Pool({ connectionString: env.databaseUrl, max: 5, types });
  return shared;
}

/** Run one parameterized query on the shared pool and return its rows. */
export async function sql<T extends pg.QueryResultRow = pg.QueryResultRow>(
  text: string,
  params: unknown[] = [],
): Promise<T[]> {
  const res = await pool().query<T>(text, params);
  return res.rows;
}

/** A separate, already-connected client (its own session) for race tests: caller must `await c.end()`. */
export async function newConnection(): Promise<pg.Client> {
  const c = new pg.Client({ connectionString: env.databaseUrl, types });
  await c.connect();
  return c;
}

export async function closePool(): Promise<void> {
  if (shared) {
    const p = shared;
    shared = undefined;
    await p.end();
  }
}

import { z } from 'zod'
import { generateSchedule, type ScheduledInvoice } from '@/lib/billing'
import { badRequest, forbidden, notFound, withRetry } from '@/lib/errors'
import { prisma } from '@/lib/prisma'
import { loadCaller, requireLeaseAccess, requireMember } from '@/server/access'
import {
  compareAllocationOrder,
  isoDateToDb,
  paidByInvoice,
  serializeInvoice,
  serializeLease,
  serializePayment,
  type InvoiceDto,
  type LeaseDto,
  type PaymentDto,
  type ServiceCtx,
} from './serialize'

const ISO_DATE = /^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$/

const createLeaseSchema = z
  .object({
    unitId: z.string().uuid(),
    tenantId: z.string().uuid(),
    startDate: z.string().regex(ISO_DATE, 'must be YYYY-MM-DD'),
    endDate: z.string().regex(ISO_DATE, 'must be YYYY-MM-DD'),
    monthlyRentSen: z.number().int().positive(),
    depositSen: z.number().int().nonnegative(),
  })
  .strict()

export type CreateLeaseInput = z.infer<typeof createLeaseSchema>

// D2 order for POST /api/leases: the route calls this before reading the body, so a non-manager gets 403
// even when the body is malformed JSON. createLease repeats the check, so it is safe to call alone.
export async function requireLeaseCreator(ctx: ServiceCtx): Promise<void> {
  requireMember(await loadCaller(ctx.userId), ['manager'])
}

export async function createLease(ctx: ServiceCtx, input: unknown): Promise<{ id: string }> {
  const caller = await loadCaller(ctx.userId)
  // POST /api/leases has no target record yet, so the role check (403) precedes body validation (400).
  const { orgId } = requireMember(caller, ['manager'])
  const body = createLeaseSchema.parse(input)

  // R11/R46: the schedule comes only from billing.ts; its validation errors are the 400 message.
  let schedule: ScheduledInvoice[]
  try {
    schedule = generateSchedule(body)
  } catch (e) {
    throw badRequest(e instanceof Error ? e.message : 'Invalid lease')
  }

  // R39/D15: body ids are untrusted; a unit or tenant outside the caller's org is a 404, exactly like a
  // nonexistent one, so another org's ids are never confirmed. The composite FKs enforce the same in the DB.
  const [unit, tenant] = await Promise.all([
    prisma.units.findFirst({ where: { id: body.unitId, org_id: orgId }, select: { id: true } }),
    prisma.tenants.findFirst({ where: { id: body.tenantId, org_id: orgId }, select: { id: true } }),
  ])
  if (!unit) throw notFound('Unit not found')
  if (!tenant) throw notFound('Tenant not found')

  // R46: lease + exactly the scheduled invoices + audit row commit together or not at all. Overlap is
  // enforced by the leases_no_overlap EXCLUDE constraint (D16): a concurrent overlapping insert waits,
  // then fails with 23P01, which errors.ts maps to 409. withRetry covers a deadlock (40P01) once.
  return withRetry(() =>
    prisma.$transaction(async (tx) => {
      const lease = await tx.leases.create({
        data: {
          org_id: orgId,
          unit_id: body.unitId,
          tenant_id: body.tenantId,
          start_date: isoDateToDb(body.startDate),
          end_date: isoDateToDb(body.endDate),
          monthly_rent_sen: body.monthlyRentSen,
          deposit_sen: body.depositSen,
          created_by: caller.userId,
        },
        select: { id: true },
      })

